    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445-a2">

                <pb facs="0795" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg701"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 74.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Lawton to
                        Lieutenant Dapray.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 11,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Prisoners are in custody of Mexican authorities and are being tried by Mexican
                    court. They were to-day separated and are allowed no communication with each
                    other or with the outside. Consular agent here states that Mexican authorities
                    have acted satisfactorily in every particular. No official demand has yet been
                    made by our Government for the prisoners, although Mexican authorities have
                    expressed their willingness to turn them over on extradition or otherwise. All
                    is quiet. There is no disagreement between officials of the two Governments and
                    no trouble can occur. Governor Torres has notified me he will visit my camp
                    to-day.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Lawton</hi></signed>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Captain.</hi></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <head>[First indorsement.]</head>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Department of Arizona</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Los Angeles, Cal.</hi></placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1887-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >March</hi> 14, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                    <p>Respectfully forwarded to headquarters Division of the Pacific.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson A.
                            Miles</hi></signed>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier-General,
                            Commanding</hi></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <head>[Second indorsement.]</head>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Division of the Pacific</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">San Francisco, Cal.</hi></placeName>, <date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1887-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March
                                    17</hi>, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                    <p>Respectfully forwarded to the Adjutant-General of the Army.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O. O. Howard</hi></signed>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Major-General, Commanding</hi></closer>
                </postscript>
                <postscript>
                    <head>[Third indorsement.]</head>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">War
                                Department</hi>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-03-26"><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">March</hi> 26,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                    <p>Official copy respectfully furnished for the information of the honorable the
                        Secretary of State.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. C. Endicott</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Secretary of War.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
